## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to craft DP with a left-anchored subarray value and exact block counts, plus reconstruction for endpoints.

## Key Concepts
- Partition DP with exactly k blocks
- Precomputation of bestStartAt[l][i]
- Reconstructing block boundaries via parent pointers
- Time/space trade-offs and potential optimizations

## Code Example
```javascript
function computeBestStartDP(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const pref = Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for (let i=0;i<n;i++) pref[i+1] = pref[i] + A[i];
  const bestStart = Array.from({length:n}, ()=> Array(n).fill(-Infinity));
  for (let l=0; l<n; l++) {
    let best = -Infinity;
    for (let i=l; i<n; i++) {
      const sum = pref[i+1]-pref[l];
      best = Math.max(best, sum);
      bestStart[l][i] = best;
    }
  }
  const dp = Array.from({length:n}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({length:n}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for (let i=0; i<n; i++) dp[i][1] = bestStart[0][i];
  for (let t=2; t<=k; t++) {
    for (let i=t-1; i<n; i++) {
      let bestVal = -Infinity, bestL = -1;
      for (let l=t-1; l<=i; l++) {
        const prev = (l-1>=0) ? dp[l-1][t-1] : (t-1===0 ? 0 : -Infinity);
        const val = prev + bestStart[l][i];
        if (val > bestVal) { bestVal = val; bestL = l; }
      }
      dp[i][t] = bestVal;
      par[i][t] = bestL;
    }
  }
  return {dp, par};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you optimize space to O(nk)?
- How would you reconstruct the exact endpoints efficiently?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to model multi-block dynamic programming with non-trivial block scoring that depends on range statistics (max, min) and block length. It also covers reconstruction of the exact blocks, and invites discussion of time/space trade-offs.

## Key Concepts

- Partition DP with fixed k blocks
- Block score uses range (max-min) and length
- Inline maintenance of max/min while expanding the last block
- Path reconstruction with predecessor pointers

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxScore(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const parent = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));

  dp[0][0] = 0;

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      let curMax = -INF, curMin = INF;
      for (let l = i; l >= 1; l--) {
        curMax = Math.max(curMax, A[l-1]);
        curMin = Math.min(curMin, A[l-1]);
        const blockScore = (curMax - curMin) * (i - l + 1);
        if (dp[l-1][t-1] + blockScore > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = dp[l-1][t-1] + blockScore;
          parent[i][t] = l-1;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct blocks
  const blocks = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (t > 0) {
    const l = parent[i][t] + 1;
    blocks.unshift([l, i]);
    i = l - 1;
    t--;
  }

  return {maxScore: dp[n][k], blocks};
}
```

## Time/Space Complexity

Time: O(n²k) - for each i and t, we scan O(n) possible l values while maintaining max/min.

Space: O(nk) for dp table plus O(nk) for parent pointers if reconstruction needed, otherwise O(nk).

## Why This Is Asked
Scheduling perspective: minimize peak workload across days; the DP is a straightforward partition DP with a range max cost. It tests understanding of maintaining running max within inner loop and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- DP over prefixes
- Range max within an inner loop
- Path reconstruction via cut[]
- Edge cases: empty input, large n, identical durations

## Code Example
```javascript
function minCostPartition(L){
  const n=L.length;
  const dp=new Array(n+1).fill(Infinity);
  const cut=new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  dp[0]=0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    let curMax=0;
    for(let k=1;k<=i;k++){
      curMax = Math.max(curMax, L[i-k]);
      const val = dp[i-k] + curMax;
      if(val < dp[i]){ dp[i] = val; cut[i] = k; }
    }
  }
  const days=[];
  let i=n;
  while(i>0){
    const k=cut[i];
    days.push(L.slice(i-k, i));
    i -= k;
  }
  days.reverse();
  return {cost: dp[n], days};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt for a 2D grid of tasks with row/day semantics?
- Can you optimize the inner loop to O(n) using a data structure for range max?

## Why This Is Asked
